WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.480
I'll teach you guys again.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.490
Your skills are simply tools of the trade.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.130
Don't you dare impose your sense of 
justice on me when you're only my tool.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.990
It's revolting!

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.120
Your breath stinks, you damn pig!

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.550
You're right. We don't know anything 
about joining society.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.230
That's why we want to learn 
here and start fresh.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.800
We want to gain a lot of knowledge.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.310
By the way, what was it 
that you said earlier?

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.680
When, exactly, did we become your tools?

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.310
Don't act like you own us, you pig!

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.450
If you want to go back to the 
world where power is everything,

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.820
then by all means, go.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.060
But you'll have to beat me first.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.510
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.790
<b>A Fool</b>

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.790
You'll have to beat me first.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.790
Master!

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.220
What are you doing here?

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.730
I wanted to watch you guys fighting up close!

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.620
Hey, hey, can you say that line one more time?

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.520
The one from the end of the last episode.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.490
If you want to go back to the 
world where power is everything,

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:49.950
then by all means, go.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.140
But you'll have to beat me first.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.820
So cool!

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.190
Don't spoil the mood!

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.200
It hurts, Master!

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.210
What are you babbling about?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.110
Hold it, fat-ass!

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.550
Why, Master?

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.150
I don't like being stuck here.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:20.050
No. Don't move from there.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.350
And definitely don't look at me.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.740
Aww...

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.210
Understood?

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.070
Yes.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.080
Sheesh...

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.480
You sure about that?

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.400
I told you about him, didn't I?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.480
He's easily influenced.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.160
If he were to begin mimicking our movements,

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.740
it would put a lot of stress on his body.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.890
The only way to stop that 
is to avoid making contact.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.760
What?

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:55.250
I guess even you worry about people, huh?

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.000
What does that mean?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.260
You guys need to shut up already!

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.360
I know! I'll give you 
something good as payment

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.650
for that nice little farce you showed me!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.660
You remember this, right?

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:30.840
This is...

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.050
You always used it for work, right?

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:38.170
It's a fast-acting poison that can 
take out any number of targets.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:41.380
Why do you have this?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.360
You couldn't make it on your own.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:45.800
What's the meaning of this?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.300
I had someone else make it, obviously.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.660
A man who knows all there 
is to know about poisons,

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.630
who has unique means of creating them,

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.310
and who can make poisons of all types.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.820
You know him well, right?

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:04.560
He's the greatest tool I've got.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.310
And he works for me.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:13.680
I don't know why, but I just remembered 
some stupid stuff from my past.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.090
<b>Herbs</b>

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.980
Welcome.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.080
Are you the herbalist 
everybody's talking about?

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.090
You're coming with me.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.960
Fix that door.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.100
I'm glad you came without any trouble 
so we didn't have to make a fuss.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.500
Well, who knows what you'll do if I disobey?

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.150
You're those mafia guys everyone's 
talking about lately, right?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.490
What do you want with me?

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:49.240
I want your skills as an herbalist.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.500
Of course, I won't ask you to do it for free.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.080
We'll pay off all your debts.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.080
My, my.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.250
You can't keep borrowing more 
money and running forever, right?

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.340
How did you know about that?

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.240
And that's how you ended up here?

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.560
Unbelievable.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:14.570
If they came after me here on top of 
the debt collectors, I'd be doomed.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:16.480
If I can hide in here and make my medicines,

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.530
that's lucky for me.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:22.600
It's true that ever since you came,
work's gotten easier.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.110
Commercial drugs can be tracked.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:29.030
And it's helpful that you supply us 
with drugs tailor-made for our jobs.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:33.980
My job is to sit here and make 
what they tell me to make.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:37.410
Since I'm not out in the open 
actually working, life's easy.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:44.670
It's a cowardly job where even if someone 
around me dies, it doesn't affect me.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:49.400
I'm taking others' lives 
to keep my own life going.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.680
But you're not doing the killing yourself.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.380
We're the ones who do the killing, 
using the things you make.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:06:59.830
I think not.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:06.190
I can tell you've never killed a man.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:11.690
You can trick the nose into 
smelling blood or people,

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:14.060
but you can't trick it into smelling death.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:20.380
I always make the same 
sleeping drug you ask for.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.950
It can't kill anyone.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.360
What do you do with the targets 
once they fall asleep?

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:30.700
If you're letting them go...

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.720
Someday, you'll get caught.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.860
What's someone like you doing here, anyway?

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.480
You ain't cut out for this.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.840
It's none of your business.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.200
Yeah, I guess not.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.740
He was brought here, just like you were.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.430
Of course, his reason why 
was nothing like yours.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:04.500
You awake, qigong boy?

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:08.170
I don't know much about qigong,

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.620
but don't put too much stress on your body.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.570
Be quiet.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:15.290
I'm not a minor leader like you.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.140
There's no need to worry about me.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.190
Harsh.

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:22.020
So what were you saying?

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:26.160
You said you were here 
to keep yourself alive,

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:27.530
but he's different.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.840
He's here to keep someone else alive.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.220
Someone else?

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.330
But he picked the wrong person to follow,

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.140
and the wrong path to do that.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.790
He's a fool.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:43.620
Sensei!

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.040
Sensei!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.360
Why is it that martial artists think

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.050
their half-assed sense of justice 
makes them so important?

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.800
I just asked him for a little help.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.810
"A fist that exists to protect," my ass.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.820
He couldn't protect a thing.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:08.060
So why does he train his body?
Or his mind?

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.800
It isn't to protect others.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.800
It's to protect himself.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:16.570
What is it you really want 
to protect right now?

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.540
Your life, or the lives of others?

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.080
Tell me.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.280
Sensei!

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.720
Are you okay, Sensei?

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.210
Get out of here!

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.280
I'll never let Sensei go with you!

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.520
I like those eyes of yours...

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.050
A lot more than your sensei's.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:38.910
Hey, kid.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:42.470
I'm about to tell you what a human really is.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.380
Shut up!

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:46.980
I've got nothing to learn from scum like you!

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.810
Sensei!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:52.350
I'm about to kill you and your students,

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:53.900
and burn down your temple.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.350
If you want to survive,

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.550
and protect your students and your temple,

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:03.290
and that oh-so-important history of yours,

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.270
give me that kid.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.740
Don't worry.

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.070
I won't kill him.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:12.710
I'll just have him do the 
job you were going to do.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.260
You understand, right?

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:20.050
You can save everything,
and the only cost is this kid!

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.210
Screw that! I'm not going to—

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.710
We can survive?

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:28.060
We can survive if we do that?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.810
Yeah, I promise.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:35.070
Please! Save us!

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.540
Ain't that great, kid?

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.590
You obeyed the teachings.

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:43.200
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.200
The one who's wrong here is the weak 
human who talked about saving others

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:52.210
while he did whatever he had 
to in order to save himself!

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:57.210
It's true that it might be best if we 
only have to sacrifice one person...

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.720
But if he was willing to sell 
out his student so easily...

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:04.980
I bet that sensei lived a nice, long life.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:08.010
I couldn't say.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:13.490
Our boss has never kept 
a promise in his life.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:20.580
To send that asshole, out of 
all the people he could've sent...

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:35.230
No way!

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:36.480
I told you,

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:39.510
I'll make medicines, but not poison!

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:40.880
Poison?

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.440
I'm telling you to make drugs.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:45.260
Our own original drug.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.260
This is poison!

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.140
It's the worst poison imaginable!

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.770
It wrecks a man's mind, body, and life!

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:56.000
If I make something like that,
I'm basically killing them myse—

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.740
Don't talk about your stupid 
sense of justice now.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:08.620
This is my...

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:12.980
No... It's something different 
mixed into what I made.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:15.490
It can't be...

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:18.250
You put the drug ingredients in my medicine?

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:21.490
Nice. You can tell just by looking, huh?

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:24.850
Your medicine sold for a ton of money.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:34.280
So it's all for money, huh?

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:39.650
You're terrible... and so am I.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:42.800
Herbalist, my ass.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.400
Don't make me laugh.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.910
So what if you know now?

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.920
Are you going to disobey 
me and end up like him?

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:54.590
You...

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:58.370
I eliminated all the people he let live.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:02.010
But that wasn't enough for 
me to stop being pissed off.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.420
I'm executing him tomorrow.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.430
What are you doing?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.900
I don't want him running off 
before the execution.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:16.370
And I don't need him or his 
tools of the trade anymore!

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.480
You can go on and on about how you're right,

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:24.570
but without power, you can't protect anything.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.520
If it was possible to live the right 
way without really meaning it,

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:30.950
villains like me would never be born!

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:39.170
Sorry...

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.520
I can't fight him head-on.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.880
So wait just a little longer.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.590
You were talking pretty big earlier!

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.600
You get to die first, shrimp!

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.100
Upa!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.600
I'll crush you!

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.370
What?!

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:02.420
Nico?

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.520
What are you doing?

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:07.860
I told you to stay out of this! 
You can't beat him!

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.560
Listen, Master...

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:12.740
There's another reason I stayed here.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.620
I wasn't sure I could go on with 
Jyugo-kun and the others.

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.100
Without my medicine, I can hardly move,

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:23.840
and my chest starts to hurt so bad.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.890
So if I stayed with them,

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:29.890
Jyugo-kun and Uno-kun would worry,
and I'd slow them down!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.140
Who the hell is he?

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.120
I don't want to cause any more trouble!

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:36.140
I feel like it would be wrong!

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.130
That's why I'm here!

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:41.160
And if I can still move...

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.190
If there's something I can do...

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.840
I want to help everyone!

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.480
That's what I thought!

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:53.410
Why?

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:58.660
Because I want to be a cool 
hero like you, Master!

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:01.250
Like me?

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:05.710
That's...

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:10.350
Looks like you were lucky enough 
to not breathe in that poison,

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:13.990
but this many poison needles 
will surely kill you!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.270
Too bad, brat!

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:19.770
This stuff...

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.960
What? Impossible!

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.520
I know the needles broke skin!

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:26.020
...won't work on me!

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:27.530
Seriously?

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:32.140
I'll defeat you!

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.360
Nailed it!

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:36.160
Hey, look over here!

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:39.540
Oh, shit! What do we do?

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.090
We left Nico...

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.290
We left Nico behind!

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:49.200
Hey, Jyugo, he took his 
medicine, right? Right?!

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.300
Tell me he did, please!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:55.550
No, he said he lost his bag...

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.060
What?!

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.890
Wait, wait. Calm down.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.540
What's this about?

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:02.840
Was that Nico guy sick?

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.750
Yeah, that's bad...

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:07.570
I hope he didn't collapse somewhere.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.360
That's not the problem.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.760
What's the problem, then?

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:14.510
You don't know how bad it is 
for him to lose the medicine

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.280
the old man makes for him...

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.080
Whoops!

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:26.460
Liquid poison doesn't work on you?

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:27.500
Then...

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:31.720
No!

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.090
Don't breathe it in!

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:34.430
Too late!

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.590
He already—

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.100
What?

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.100
Super...

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.690
Inazuma Kick!

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.090
Did that hit him?

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.860
Stop screwing around!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.780
I didn't expect poison to not work,

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.290
but it seems that's all 
you've got going for you.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.260
Ow...

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:06.820
Without basic strength and speed,

00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:08.800
you're useless.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.050
You're pissing me off.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:12.550
I'll kill you!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.850
What do you think you're doing?

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:17.680
Master, you can move already?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:21.560
I recovered a bit while you were facing him.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:22.890
I'm so glad!

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.490
I was useful to you!

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:27.440
Forget it. Just stay out of this.

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:32.150
<i>The way he moved was already 
similar to me and Liang.</i>

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.750
<i>I can't let this go on!</i>

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:37.220
Okay, I'll work even harder!

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.160
Wait!

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:40.830
That weapon is...

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.830
I'll blow you away!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:45.330
Liang-kun?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.820
Don't get close to him!

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:50.340
He'll blow you away!

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.090
I-It exploded?!

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:57.930
That's rigged to explode if it touches you!

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.020
You stay back!

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:00.660
We'll handle the rest—

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:03.350
Liang-kun!

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:07.100
Didn't expect that, did ya?

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.600
No, that can't be...

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:12.480
Qigong?

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.970
Rokuriki-san can't use that...

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:20.800
Attack charm talismans can do more 
than force the body to move.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:24.990
With the power of a daoshi added,
they can let you use qigong, too.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.870
If you do that...

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.710
If someone who hasn't mastered 
qigong uses it anyway,

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:33.160
it might be enough to kill them.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.540
It doesn't matter.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.840
I use everything I possibly can!

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.100
You scum!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:52.050
<i>I can't let Rokuriki-san use any more chi.</i>

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:53.110
<i>But...</i>

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:58.790
<i>If I use qigong, it will transfer to him.</i>

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:00.110
<i>But still...</i>

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.120
Thinking?

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:09.000
What do you think it is 
that's slowing you down?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.750
It's pity...

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.510
and hesitation!

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:20.500
Master!

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.800
"I'm fighting for others."
"I'm fighting to protect."

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:27.300
You come up with some reason 
to hate the obvious villain,

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:29.880
waving around your rotten sense of "justice."

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:33.190
I hate people like that!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:37.030
Master!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.780
Stay back...

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:40.780
And people like you, too!

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:45.910
You were saying something 
about medicine earlier, right?

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:49.910
I've seen lots of people like you in my work.

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:52.750
In orphanages or hospitals,
or on the side of the road.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.920
They all had the same eyes.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.690
The ones you have now.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:02.700
Limb spasms. Trouble breathing.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.800
Slow pupil response.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.620
Those are the symptoms that occur 
when medicine's about to wear off.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:12.860
I don't know why poison wouldn't 
work on someone like that.

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:15.610
Maybe you're special.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.630
It hurts... It hurts...

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:21.360
It's so bitter... So hot...

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.360
Cold... It hurts...

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.610
But it's over now.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.620
I'll kill you.

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:33.370
Where... Where are you, guys?

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:40.960
It hurts... It hurts...

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:46.120
The medicine... The medicine...

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.140
Did he finally break?

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:53.240
<i>It's like there's a bug 
moving around in my ears.</i>

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.080
<i>I don't like the pain.</i>

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:58.020
<i>I don't like the suffering.</i>

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.880
<i>I don't like the bitterness.</i>

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:01.900
<i>I don't like the hurt!</i>

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.660
Where's the medicine...

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:08.290
Please...

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.410
<b>I don't want to die</b>

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.390
<i>I don't want to die!</i>

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:12.710
<i>Someone...</i>

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:18.920
<i>Hey, did you ever hear about that dealer?</i>

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.080
It hurts... It hurts...

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:24.720
I don't like it... It's bitter...

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:26.090
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:29.680
Hurts... Bitter...

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.430
Nico!

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.430
He's dead, huh?

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:38.690
<b>He's got two personalities,
so they call him...</b>

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.600
<i>He's got two personalities,</i>

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.310
<i>so they call him...</i>

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:39.610
Nico.

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:49.650
Hello.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:27.670
Holy shit! Holy shit! This is not good!

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:29.920
When his medicine runs out, Nico goes crazy!

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:32.120
We have to save him!

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:35.850
Or it might destroy his body!

00:23:36.190 --> 00:23:38.640
Next time: "Awakening Poison."

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Awakening Poison</b>
